5. Frontend acceptance criteria

The frontend can be considered ready for its next completion review when:

All required pages and workflows are implemented.
All forms have appropriate validation and error feedback.
Bulk operations provide progress, success, and failure feedback.
Dashboards and charts display data accurately from connected APIs.
Search, filtering, and pagination work consistently.
Public and admin interfaces are responsive across screen sizes.
Accessibility checks are completed.
Frontend tests cover critical workflows and user interactions.
Production frontend build and deployment configuration are verified.

Scope note: This roadmap lists frontend work identified or implied by the audit. It does not claim that these tasks remain unimplemented in the current repository; each item should be verified against the latest code before being assigned.